**RCA:**

Bug: The two gh-922 trigger fail-open tests (`test_smAgent.js`: marker-flattening + two-rules same-tick) fail under the canonical `dmtools run` runner everywhere — including a normal checkout — reding the agents-gate in dart's shard harness (713/715).

Root cause (test defects from #923, not git ops):
1. Marker-flattening test asserts the whole marker comment body is ONE line (`markers[0].indexOf('\n') === -1`) — but `recordDispatchFailure` (js/smAgent.js) posts the reviewed multi-line shape: marker line on line 1 (required by `TRIGGER_FAIL_MARKER_RE`'s `^`-anchored reader contract: "the writer always puts the marker on its own line"), then prose. The only newline-free part is the flattened error message itself. Also `split('\n')[0].indexOf('attempt 1/3') === 0` can never hold (line 1 starts with '⚠️').
2. Two-rules test feeds the makeSmAgent items-stub a RAW /pulls payload (`{number, head:{ref}}`), but the stub's contract is the NORMALIZED source item (`{key:'pr-302', prNumber, branch, labels:[strings], ...}` — the shape `githubSource.queryPrs` produces). `recordDispatchFailure` correctly bails on `!item.prNumber || !item.branch` → 0 markers, expected 1. The test also omits the `pr:` fixture, so the park comment could never carry `parked-head: <sha>` for its later assertion.

Evidence for "same tests green in own CI": this repo's quality.yml runs the node harness marked "~108 known mock-gap failures... a red harness must not block" — the two failures surfaced there too but were non-blocking. The shard harness runs the canonical runner, where they block.

Fix approach (tests only, product code already correct):
1. Marker-flattening test: assert the actual contract — line 1 is the marker line (`⚠️ trigger-failed <branch> — attempt 1/3 ...`), the injected `attempt 3/3` text is absent from the body, `triggerFailMarks` parses 1, and the body is exactly [marker line, prose line] — i.e. the multi-line ERROR was flattened into the prose line (the injected '\n' is gone).
2. Two-rules test: normalize the fixture item (tfSourceItem helper) and provide `pr: {number: 302, head: {sha}}` so the park comment carries the parked-head sha.

